026-07-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"},{"bioguideId":"L000560","fullName":"Rep. Larsen, Rick [D-WA-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"},{"bioguideId":"T000487","fullName":"Rep. Tokuda, Jill N. [D-HI-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"},{"bioguideId":"K000398","fullName":"Rep. Kean, Thomas H. [R-NJ-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"D000623","fullName":"Rep. DeSaulnier, Mark [D-CA-10]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T20:05:35+00:00","id":"hr1685-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-27","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-02-03","text":"Subcommittee Hearings Held"},"laws":[],"number":"1685","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"F000466","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. Fitzpatrick, Brian K. [R-PA-1]","party":"R","state":"PA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-27","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Justice for ALS Veterans Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill extends increased dependency and indemnity compensation to the surviving spouse of a veteran who dies from amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS or Lou Gehrig's disease) regardless of how long the veteran had such disease prior to death. Under current law, such compensation is paid for a service-connected disability that was rated totally disabling for a continuous period of at least eight years immediately preceding death.</p><p>For purposes of compensation for a surviving spouse of a veteran who dies from ALS, the spouse must have been married to the veteran for a continuous period of eight years or longer prior to the death of the veteran.</p><p>Additionally, the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) must report on service-connected disabilities the VA determines should be treated in the same manner as ALS for purposes of dependency and indemnity compensation.</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-08T16:12:49Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Justice for ALS Veterans Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-08-18T08:05:40Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-08-18T08:05:40Z"}
